# SilverBullet — the keys stored in secrets.sops.json, one value each (`sopsgen
# apply` fills generated ones, `sopsedit` the rest). Values built from other
# secrets live in env.nix. Key set must match secrets.sops.json and
# tests/fixtures/stacks/silverbullet.sops.json.
# Both services share this one file, so each sees the other's key — mind that
# before adding a name SilverBullet would recognise.

# Git mirror
# Forgejo repo the space is mirrored to, credentials in the URL:
#   http://<forgejo-user>:<PAT>@127.0.0.1:10550/<owner>/<repo>.git
# http + loopback on purpose — the sidecar is host-networked, so the PAT never
# leaves the host and nothing depends on DNS, TLS, Caddy or the tailnet.
# Operator steps: create the repo (private) by hand; Settings -> Applications ->
# Generate Token with `write:repository` ONLY; paste it here.
# Until it is real, git-sync.sh detects `changeme` and alerts hourly instead of
# pretending to mirror. Conflict rule is REMOTE-WINS — read git-sync.sh first.
GIT_SYNC_REMOTE=http://changeme_forgejo_user:changeme_forgejo_pat@127.0.0.1:10550/changeme_owner/changeme_repo.git
